## Previously raised findings (review-round registry)

These defects were raised on earlier review rounds of this PR. For each finding below: verify fixed (cite the fixing hunk), withdraw (reason required), or mark re-introduced. New claims need new evidence — a claim already on this list is answered, not re-raised.

| id | status | severity | file | claim |
|----|--------|----------|------|-------|
| F1 | open | IMPORTANT | lib/src/compaction/structured/engine.dart | ⚠️ important ac1 one basis invariant has a reachable counterexample — boundary less windowed resumes re arm phantom anchors through refreshagentstate the fix makes the projection the single anchor authority and resetstaleusageanchors session tree dart 874 886 resets only entries before the last boundary record compactionrecord hiddenrangerecord compactcheckpointrecord a resident tail that contains no boundary record returns staleentryids const so the rebuild at this line re arms every persisted generation time usage anchor — exactly the anchors the cli s resume path deliberately zeroed one line after loading lib src cli session commands dart 962 — agent state messages resetloadedusageanchors messages with the comment loaded usage anchors are generation time post compaction they phantom report the pre compaction size 183k on a 27k branch and fire a no op compaction on every resume re anchor at chars 4 the divergent sequence a windowed resume whose boundary walk exhausts maxpages session commands dart logs boundary walk exhausted maxpages proceeding with the tail window leaves a boundary less giant tail the resume zeroes anchors → the gate arms on the chars 4 basis the engine s refresh at this line then re arms the persisted phantom anchor → estimaterequesttokens anchors at the pre trim size token estimation dart 489 493 — any anchor suppresses the overhead addend and prices the whole request engine basis ≠ gate basis — the gh 2237 divergence class opposite direction the engine chases the phantom number folds hides far past the real over amount and burns hide checkpoint provider passes until a fold s own hiddenrangerecord lands a boundary and re collapses the basis cost is bounded one over aggressive fold self healing hides are expandable — that is why this is ⚠️ not 🚨 — but the pr s headline claim the engine cannot re derive a different basis than the gate that armed it pr description ac1 is falsified on this path and no test pins it ut 2 requires a boundary e2 requires no anchors at all the boundary less windowed resume case is exactly the gap between them ask either extend the stale anchor curation to cover load time anchors whose generation context the resident tail cannot vouch for the resetloadedusageanchors rationale applied at projection level for boundary less tails or state in refreshagentstate s contract why the boundary less resume basis is acceptable and pin the decision with a ut gate basis vs engine basis after a maxpages exhausted resume no boundary records pre fix the blanket zero made this specific path correct engine basis gate basis chars 4 please confirm the regression is intended or covered elsewhere before merge |

### How to answer

Add a `findingReview` block to `outputs/pr_review.json` (alongside `inlineComments`):

```json
{"findingReview": {
  "dispositions": [
    {"n": 1, "status": "fixed", "hunk": "<file:lines \u2014 the fixing hunk>"},
    {"n": 2, "status": "withdrawn", "reason": "<why this is not a defect>"},
    {"n": 3, "status": "re-introduced"}
  ],
  "confirmations": [
    {"proposedFor": 1, "same": true}
  ]
}}
```

Unconfirmed candidates become new identities (the merge bias is confirm-only); a genuinely new finding on a resolved item is expected to be raised again with new evidence.

# PR new hunks — what changed since the last review concluded

Last reviewed head: 34629911c2b557fef48b41d45a9c5163a778ba27
Current head: 93770c08aebdd97a9cd2db9fc38b6269590a0d30

These hunks are the re-review scope, together with their interaction
neighborhood (direct callers/callees of changed symbols). Every line
NOT shown here is frozen: a finding on an unchanged line must show that
these hunks make the problem worse (the interaction test) — otherwise
it is advisory digest only, never a review thread.

